## 1. History is garden-worthy

Today's API can tell us:

> QMI8658C costs $0.74 today.

It probably cannot reliably tell us:

```text
Sep 2026   $0.74   182k stock
Dec 2026   $0.63   311k
Jun 2027   $0.48   780k
Dec 2027   $0.31   1.4m
```

That historical curve becomes valuable.

But we don't need hourly snapshots of 8 million capacitors.

Create **observation tiers**.

```text
TIER 0 — identity only
millions of catalogue entities
refresh rarely

TIER 1 — monthly
interesting technology categories

TIER 2 — daily
strategic components / active BOMs

TIER 3 — hourly/event-driven
identified bottlenecks or anomalies
```

A generic 10k resistor probably stays Tier 0 forever.

A new cheap robot actuator controller might jump immediately to Tier 2.

This makes the garden manageable.

